## 16. First 90 days: validation plan

The objective is not to build the entire platform. It is to discover one
workflow that buyers will pay to improve.

### Days 1--30: discover

-   [ ] Select two or three candidate workflow categories.
-   [ ] Interview 15--20 buyers and frontline users.
-   [ ] Map the current workflow, tools, handoffs, exceptions and
    approval points.
-   [ ] Estimate current cost, turnaround time, rework and error impact.
-   [ ] Identify data access, security and procurement requirements.
-   [ ] Score candidate workflows and choose one initial wedge.

### Days 31--60: test

-   [ ] Obtain written authorization for representative pilot data.
-   [ ] Build a narrow prototype: ingestion → extraction → validation →
    review → output → audit.
-   [ ] Create an expert-reviewed evaluation set.
-   [ ] Measure quality, false negatives, processing time, human review
    and cost.
-   [ ] Demonstrate the prototype to the economic buyer and actual
    users.
-   [ ] Present a priced pilot with explicit acceptance criteria.

### Days 61--90: sell and decide

-   [ ] Secure one or two paid pilots, or a clearly documented
    procurement path with a committed buyer.
-   [ ] Agree on scope, data processing, ownership, evaluation and exit
    criteria.
-   [ ] Review the results against the original baseline.
-   [ ] Decide to proceed, revise the wedge or stop.
-   [ ] Do not expand to a second industry before the first workflow has
    passed its gate.

